---
/**
 * One activity's counts strip — /activities/{slug}/, from the activity-page
 * design handoff, 14 Sep 2026: how many took part, how many facilitated, how
 * many watched. The home page's `.homecounts` strip (HeroMeta.astro,
 * components.css) with one activity's own numbers, sitting directly under the
 * hero.
 *
 * ⛔ MODELLED ON SpaceCounts.astro, NOT AN EXTENSION OF IT — the handoff's own
 * instruction, and the same call SpaceCounts itself made against HeroMeta.
 * Those four items and their keys are the home page's; these three are an
 * activity's. Same classes, so no new CSS.
 *
 * ⛔⛔ THIS PUTS ATTENDANCE ABOVE THE WRITE-UP, WHICH REVERSES THE OWNER'S
 * RULING OF 22 AUG 2026 — recorded verbatim in activities/[slug].astro, where
 * the reversal is dated and attributed. Reversed BY THE OWNER, 14 Sep 2026,
 * after seeing the spaces pages. Not a builder's preference, and not a
 * decision this component may re-take.
 *
 * Rules carried over from the old `.attendance` chips UNCHANGED — none of them
 * is re-opened by the move, and none may be re-litigated here:
 * ⛔ ZERO RENDERS NOTHING, PER ITEM. 0 does not mean nobody facilitated, it
 * means nobody typed a number, and a reader cannot tell those apart. A null
 * was already suppressed; the `> 0` filter below covers both at once.
 * ⛔⛔ THE STRIP IS ALWAYS PRESENT AS OF 16 Sep 2026, AND THAT REVERSES THE RULE
 * THIS COMMENT USED TO STATE. It said "IF NO COUNT HAS A VALUE THE WHOLE STRIP
 * IS ABSENT" and made the caller test it. The strip now also carries the page's
 * two actions — copy-link and download-the-card — at its right end, so an
 * absent strip means a reader loses both controls because nobody typed an
 * attendance figure. Owner's ruling, 16 Sep 2026, asked and answered directly.
 * ⭐ What is unchanged: an empty COUNTS LIST renders nothing — no heading over
 * an empty row, no dash, no "0 took part". The <ul> simply is not emitted. The
 * per-item `> 0` filter below is untouched.
 * ⚠️ 0 of 253 published activities have no counts today, so nothing exercises
 * this path yet. It exists for the first activity an editor saves without them.
 * ⚠️ FIXED ORDER, NEVER SORTED BY VALUE: took part, facilitators, watched.
 * Sorting by value makes the same page reorder itself between visits.
 * ⛔ THE FIGURE AND ITS LABEL ARE ONE STRING TO A SCREEN READER — "10 took
 * part". No aria-hidden on the number, no separate label, no splitting the two
 * across elements. The figure is split out at `{n}` ONLY so it can be styled.
 *
 * ⛔ NOTHING HERE IS A LINK, so nothing is underlined — unlike SpaceCounts,
 * whose activities figure links `?space=`. All three take the same ink and
 * weight (`.homecounts__n`), because what separates items on this site is what
 * is clickable, and here nothing is. ⚠️ Do not give one of them a destination
 * without the others: that is the owner's ruling of 25 Aug 2026 (HeroMeta).
 *
 * ⭐ THE WORDS LIVE IN DIRECTUS — `activities.counts.participants|
 * facilitators|audience`, each "{n} label", and each with a `_one` twin for
 * the singular: t() has no plural support and "1 Facilitators" shipped on
 * every activity page once already. The pick is made HERE, in code, on
 * `n === 1`. No markup is ever built from a Directus value, and a `{n}` an
 * editor deletes drops the figure and leaves the label.
 * ⛔ ALL SIX KEYS ALSO EXIST IN `scripts/ui-strings.json` — a key that lives
 * only in Directus renders as its own name against a fresh or restored
 * instance, and the warning for that is DEV-gated, so a production build fails
 * silently.
 * ⚠️ Their Malayalam is deliberately EMPTY, not machine Malayalam: the seeder
 * treats empty as absent and English shows until the owner approves a wording
 * per key. Standing rule.
 *
 * ⚠️ FROZEN AT BUILD TIME, like every other count on this site. If that stops
 * being acceptable the fix is a rebuild, not a browser fetch.
 */
import { DEFAULT_LOCALE, type Locale } from '../lib/i18n';
import { getT } from '../lib/content';

interface Props {
  locale?: string;
  /** `as_activity.attendance` — `null` means nobody recorded it, NOT zero. */
  participants: number | null;
  facilitators: number | null;
  audience: number | null;
}
const { locale, participants, facilitators, audience } = Astro.props;
const loc = (locale as Locale) ?? DEFAULT_LOCALE;
const t = await getT(loc);

/* ⭐ Indian digit grouping on both locales — the same formatter HeroMeta and
   SpaceCounts use. Unreachable above 999 on today's real attendance figures;
   consistent with the rest of the site regardless. */
const nf = new Intl.NumberFormat(loc === 'ml' ? 'ml-IN' : 'en-IN');

function item(key: string, value: number | null) {
  const n = value ?? 0;
  const [before, ...rest] = t(n === 1 ? `${key}_one` : key).split('{n}');
  return { before, figure: rest.length > 0 ? nf.format(n) : null, after: rest.join('{n}'), n };
}
const items = [
  item('activities.counts.participants', participants),
  item('activities.counts.facilitators', facilitators),
  item('activities.counts.audience', audience),
].filter(({ n }) => n > 0);
---

<div class="homecounts">
  <div class="wrap wrap--wide homecounts__row">
    {
      /* ⛔ The list is omitted entirely when nothing was counted, rather than
         rendered empty — an empty <ul> is still a list to a screen reader. The
         actions in the slot below are what keep the strip worth drawing. */
      items.length > 0 && (
        <ul class="homecounts__list">
          {items.map(({ before, figure, after }) => (
            <li>
              {before}
              {figure && <span class="homecounts__n">{figure}</span>}
              {after}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      )
    }
    {/* Pushed to the right end by `margin-left:auto` on .homecounts__actions —
        so with no counts they sit alone on the row, still right-aligned. */}
    <div class="homecounts__actions"><slot name="actions" /></div>
  </div>
</div>
